{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is our current best at 0.713 acc / 0.695 F1, beating the best RNA-only model (config_006, 0.653) by ~6 points. However, the image modality alone with resnet50 was very weak (config_010: 0.208), raising uncertainty about whether the image branch is contributing meaningful signal or merely adding noise. Question: Does a substantially stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs. resnet50) improve the multimodal model, or is the image modality's contribution limited regardless of encoder quality? config_039 changes only the image encoder relative to config_033, isolating this single variable. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean one-variable extension of our best configuration, directly tests whether the image modality has untapped representational capacity, and the answer will determine whether future budget should invest in image-encoder variants or pivot to other design axes (RNA encoder, aggregation). A large gain would validate the multimodal direction and guide further image-side exploration; a small or null gain would indicate the image modality's ceiling is low, redirecting effort to RNA-side or fusion improvements."
}

